    "Picture Source": "MiLB.com",
    "Notes Updated": "11/20/2024",
    "Scouting Notes": "I still think he can stick at third. Can make off platform throws at his size, very impressive athlete.\n Does need to clean up some of the actions, and gets a bit too loose over there at times, making off balance throws for no reason\n Still a huge ceiling with the bat\n The patience has now shown to be more passive than patient for me. His in zone swing rate was as low as anybody in all of MiLB. Need to find a balance between patience and aggressiveness.\n Aggressiveness could really help him tap into the pop he has. Right now, a lot more raw power than game power\n EV's into the 112+ range\n Still stole a lot of bases, but probably an average runner in terms of speed, maybe slightly faster.\n Very good athlete for his size.\n Extremely willing to take HBP's which I love, and view as a legit skill that will always be able to boost his OBP.",
    "Notes Updated 2": "9/10/2023",
    "Scouting Notes 2": "Swing is really starting to remind me of Hunter Pence. It's weird, but I see no reason it doesn't work\n  I think he can stick at third. Can make off platform throws at his size, very impressive athlete.\n  Bat is legit. Huge upside here. Needs to curb the infield pop ups (and has recently)\n  Verypatient approach with way less swing and miss than you'd expect with his swing and the moving parts.\n  Possibly too patient, which is something I'll be watching next year\n  Want to see him at High  A and above, but this could be an absolute steal for the Brewers",
    "Notes Updated 3": "7/30/2022",
    "Scouting Notes 3": "Post Draft 2022\n  Funky looking swing, like a combination of Josh Donaldson and Mike Brosseau\n  Big time bat speed\n  Strong throwing arm, I think he ends up in right field.\n  Really big raw power that could be plus.Already hitting balls in triple digit exit velos.\n  Swing has some moving parts that can lead him to drop his hands swing, may cause some issues with consistency.\n  Overall, it’s a really big package of tools, that reminds me a bit of Hunter Renfroe. \n  6’4 18  year  olds that can move like Adams are not abundantly available.\n  Chance he will be able to stick at third base, but wouldn't be surprised to see a move to corner outfield.\n  Got off to a great start to pro ball statistically in a very small sample.",
    "Notes Updated 4": "N/A",
